      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَمْطَمَ</span></b>  <i>He swam in the midst of the
sea.</i> (IAar, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>It</i> (the sea) <i>became
full.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>He had a barbarousness,</i> or
<i>vitiousness,</i> or <i>an impotence,</i> or <i>impediment, in
his speech,</i> or <i>utterance, not speaking clearly,</i> or
<i>correctly.</i> (TA.)

